{
  "analysis": "The review describes a time-limited event whose reward opportunity changed while the player was away, despite the displayed remaining time. This satisfies Playing by Appointment because the event clock and schedule determine when the player must return and the player loses access to the near-completed reward. I considered FOMO but rejected it because the text describes an actual schedule-based loss, not anticipatory anxiety or pressure to keep playing. I rejected Pay to Progress because no payment is explicitly tied to overcoming the dice shortage, and rejected Waste Aversion because no stranded currency or concrete purchasable shortfall is described.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "T_PlayingByAppointment",
      "span": "it said 2Days left. Now just logged in after sleeping and the event is now changed.",
      "rationale": "The event's displayed time window and subsequent change impose a schedule and cause the player to lose the pending reward opportunity."
    }
  ],
  "invoked_web_search": false,
