{
  "analysis": "The review describes timed bonuses expiring while the player is away, which imposes a game-controlled schedule and forfeits rewards, so T_PlayingByAppointment applies. It also describes paying for more moves than were used, showing wasted in-game value, so M_WasteAversion applies. The inability to earn enough gold to continue without buying describes a paid alternative to continued play, so M_PayToProgress applies. The missing lives from a purchased package is described as a failure to deliver the purchase, which is a technical or fulfillment fault rather than a deliberate dark pattern under R11. The package being timed is mentioned as a complaint, but no qualifying subscription, expiry-pressure, or purchase-term deception is explicitly described. No other label is supported.",
  "labels": [
    {
      "label": "M_WasteAversion",
      "span": "I was charged 10 gold pcs for 5 moves, I had 2 moves left. I had 7 moves but only used 1 move.",
      "rationale": "The player describes paying for a quantity of moves that was not fully usable, demonstrating wasted in-game value."
    },
